From 97f40f2fff0425f589970d33ec87d93a66484c7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Qingfang Deng <dqfext@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:24:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] tls: Reject exhausted TX record sequences before async
 encryption

Submitting encryption before detecting record sequence exhaustion lets
an asynchronous completion race tls_advance_record_sn(). Depending on
when the callback observes sk_err, the same send can report success or
EBADMSG. The existing tls_basic.recseq_wrap selftest expects EBADMSG and
failed 9 of 30 runs with pcrypt on the previous kernel.

Reject an all-ones sequence before submitting the AEAD request. The
existing push failure path aborts the socket and frees the open record,
without a callback racing the exhaustion error.

Validation: the existing recseq_wrap selftest passed 30 consecutive
pcrypt runs in QEMU TCG with KASAN and lockdep. The focused TLS suite
passed 117 tests; kernel builds, diff checks and checkpatch passed.

OpenAI Codex assisted with diagnosis, implementation, validation and this
changelog while extending asynchronous kTLS I/O coverage.

Fixes: a42055e8d2c3 ("net/tls: Add support for async encryption of records for performance")
(cherry picked from commit 0721fa685170f0e4cf8ac390003e07c681dced40)
---
 net/tls/tls_sw.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/tls/tls_sw.c b/net/tls/tls_sw.c
index 5479db1728f6..c1b7ebe454b6 100644
--- a/net/tls/tls_sw.c
+++ b/net/tls/tls_sw.c
@@ -598,6 +598,13 @@ static int tls_do_encryption(struct sock *sk,
 	struct scatterlist *sge = sk_msg_elem(msg_en, start);
 	int rc, iv_offset = 0;
 
+	/* Reject exhaustion before handing the record to an async cipher.
+	 * Otherwise tls_advance_record_sn() races the completion callback:
+	 * send may succeed or fail depending on when sk_err becomes visible.
+	 */
+	if (!memchr_inv(tls_ctx->tx.rec_seq, 0xff, prot->rec_seq_size))
+		return -EBADMSG;
+
 	/* For CCM based ciphers, first byte of IV is a constant */
 	switch (prot->cipher_type) {
 	case TLS_CIPHER_AES_CCM_128:
